.TH MANTA-SIZE 1 "manta-size v1.0.0" "Manta Tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
manta-size \- analyze directory sizes from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B size [options] [path]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively calculate directory sizes with human-readable output, sorting, depth control, and file-type filtering. Zero external dependencies.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B path
Directory or file to analyze (default: current directory)
.TP
.B -d, --depth N
Maximum recursion depth (default: 1)
.TP
.B -t, --type EXT
Filter by file extension (e.g. .py, .md)
.TP
.B --no-sort
Disable sorting by size
.TP
.B --raw
Output raw bytes instead of human-readable
.TP
.B --version
Show version and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Analyze current directory
.B size
.TP
Deep scan (3 levels)
.B size -d 3 /var/log
.TP
Only Python files
.B size -t .py src/
.TP
Raw bytes output
.B size --raw /tmp
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Path does not exist or cannot be read
